# Build output. Regenerated by `npm run build` and by the release pipeline
# (ROADMAP.md section 18: the released ZIP ships compiled assets).
/build/

# Dependencies resolved by tooling. The released ZIP must not depend on the
# merchant running npm or Composer, so neither directory is part of the package.
/node_modules/
/vendor/

# Tool caches.
/.npm-cache/
/.phpcs-cache
/.phpunit.result.cache
/.phpstan-cache/

# Deliberately NOT ignored: the planning package under roadmap/.
#
# It is the record of what was asked for. The validation documents cite it by
# section number, the backlog is the order the work was done in, and an audit of
# the result is only possible against the request it answered. Versioning the code
# while discarding the specification would leave every "why is it like this"
# question unanswerable from the repository alone.
#
# The same goes for docs/, examples/ and the two lock files: they are part of the
# record, not derived output.
